            <ArticleTitle>Transplantation tolerance: the big picture. Where do we stand, where should we go?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>135-137</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/cei.12933</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A major goal in organ transplantation has been to safely exploit the natural processes of immune tolerance in order to minimize the dose and duration of drug immunosuppression. In this commentary, I argue that we can learn from how tumours avoid rejection, to evolve a three-stage tolerance-inducing strategy for transplanted tissues.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 British Society for Immunology.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
